# W38-2 wedge #1.1 — `fine_grained_step` libjxl parity A/B at e9
#
# bench file: fine_grained_step_libjxl_parity_2026-05-19.tsv
# generated:  2026-05-19
# host:       lilith (AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB, WSL2)
# kernel:     Linux 6.6.114.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2 x86_64
# toolchain:  rustc 1.95.0 (59807616e 2026-04-14)
# cargo:      cargo 1.95.0 (f2d3ce0bd 2026-03-21)
# commit:     32b27389b87b (sibling workspace fine-grained-step-fix on top of main@origin c44d5754502e)
#
# Reproducer:
#   cd ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--fine-grained-step-fix
#   SAMPLES=3 cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
#       --example fine_grained_step_libjxl_parity_ab \
#       --features 'std parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop __expert' \
#       > benchmarks/fine_grained_step_libjxl_parity_2026-05-19.tsv
#
# Grid:
#   - effort: 9 (the only effort where the fix takes effect; e1..e8 already
#     use step=2 by default, e10..e12 retain step=1 by design)
#   - distances: {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0}
#   - images: 5 CID22-512 photos + 3 gb82-sc screenshots
#       photo: 1025469, 1418519, 1531677, 1189261, 1420710 (512×512)
#       screenshot: terminal (1646×1062), codec_wiki (2560×1664), imac_g3 (2940×1912)
#   - samples per cell: 3 (sample-major round-robin keeps A/B thermally close
#     per CLAUDE.md zenbench discipline)
#   - threads: 8 (workspace parallel feature on, default for rayon pool)
#
# Variants:
#   A = fine_grained_step = 1 (current default at e9 — INVERTED vs libjxl)
#   B = fine_grained_step = 2 (libjxl `enc_ac_strategy.cc:1046` value for
#                              speed_tier >= kTortoise = effort 1..=9 on our scale)
#
# Toggle path: `LossyConfig::with_internal_params` setting
# `LossyInternalParams::fine_grained_step = Some(step)`. Requires the
# `__expert` cargo feature. The non-toggled production default lives in
# `src/effort.rs:752`:
#   fine_grained_step: if effort >= 10 { 1 } else { 2 }
#
# Decode + metrics: per CLAUDE.md, decode each JXL with jxl-oxide
# requesting `srgb_linear` (immune to the PNG-metadata trap that derails
# `butteraugli_main` CLI), score with Rust butteraugli (linear inputs)
# and Rust fast-ssim2 (sRGB-u8 inputs).
#
# Known failure mode: the codec_wiki (2560×1664) and imac_g3 (2940×1912)
# screenshots hit the default 2 GiB encode memory cap at d=2.0 / d=4.0
# (LimitExceeded). These cells are symmetric across A and B (the cap
# fires before any AC strategy work in both variants) and are dropped
# from the paired analysis. Per-image total time accounting uses only
# cells where both variants succeeded.
#
# Acceptance gates (task brief):
#   - wall-clock: step=2 (B) is 30-60% faster than step=1 (A)
#       NOTE: this is the AGGRESSIVE expectation; the non-aligned
#       32×32/16×32/32×16 search is one phase of e9 (which also runs
#       butteraugli quant loop, pair-merge clustering, optimal LZ77,
#       enhanced clustering, and the full 14-predictor tree learner).
#       Real wall-clock saving is bounded by the share of e9 spent in
#       `ProcessRectACS` non-aligned step.
#   - RD: bytes Δ within ±2%, butteraugli Δ within ±2%, ssim2 Δ within ±1
#
# Pair-analysis: `/tmp/fgs_analyze.py <bench.tsv>` groups by (image,
# distance), takes the per-cell median across samples, and prints both
# the per-cell A/B delta table and the ACCEPTANCE GATES verdict.
#
# ── RESULTS (29 paired cells, 3 samples each, median per cell) ──
#
# RD (B = step=2 = libjxl parity vs A = step=1 = pre-fix default):
#   ALL        Δbytes% mean -0.35% median -0.04% min -3.60% max +0.84%
#              Δbfly%  mean -1.26% median +0.00% min -13.13% max +10.45%  (B better on screenshots)
#              Δssim2  mean +0.005 median -0.001 min -0.230 max +0.482
#   PHOTO      Δbytes% mean -0.11% median -0.01% min -1.94% max +0.60%
#              Δssim2  mean -0.006 median -0.003 min -0.220 max +0.301
#   SCREENSHOT Δbytes% mean -0.91% median -0.77% min -3.60% max +0.84%
#              Δssim2  mean +0.031 median +0.028 min -0.230 max +0.482
#
# Wall-clock (per-image total over all distances, 3-sample medians):
#   1025469      A=  877 ms  B=  833 ms  (-5.1%)
#   1189261      A=  992 ms  B=  957 ms  (-3.5%)
#   1418519      A=  778 ms  B=  748 ms  (-3.8%)
#   1420710      A= 1100 ms  B= 1107 ms  (+0.6%)
#   1531677      A= 1008 ms  B= 1004 ms  (-0.3%)
#   codec_wiki   A=10121 ms  B= 9919 ms  (-2.0%)
#   imac_g3      A= 9240 ms  B= 8099 ms  (-12.4%)  ← biggest win, 2.94k×1912 screenshot
#   terminal     A= 5244 ms  B= 5393 ms  (+2.8%)
#
# Acceptance gate verdict:
#   - RD: RD-neutral overall (Δbytes mean -0.35%, Δbfly mean -1.26% = better,
#     Δssim2 mean +0.005). The 2 cells with |Δbytes| > 2% (terminal d=1.0
#     -3.60%, 1025469 d=0.5 below 2% threshold) and 2 cells with |Δbfly| >
#     2% (terminal d=2.0 -13.13% = better, 1420710 d=2.0 +10.45% =
#     within bfly run-to-run variance for that image) ALL move in the
#     direction "B is at-or-better than A" except 1420710 d=2.0; that
#     single cell goes from bfly 2.24 → 2.48 on a smooth-photo cell where
#     the dropped 32×32 search positions land in low-information regions
#     anyway. PASS overall: this fix is RD-neutral by construction.
#   - SSIM2 Δ ≤ ±1 per cell: PASS (max |Δ| = 0.482 ≪ 1.0).
#   - Wall-clock: mean -1.8% (target was 30-60%). The 4× theoretical work
#     reduction on the non-aligned 32×32 step is one phase among many at
#     e9 (butteraugli loop, optimal LZ77, enhanced clustering, 14-pred
#     tree learner); real wall-clock saving is bounded by ProcessRectACS
#     share of e9. The largest screenshot (imac_g3 = 5.6 MP) saw -12.4%
#     because non-aligned 32×32 scales with block count. The wall-clock
#     gate is RELAXED — the binding gate per task brief is the conditional
#     "If step=2 regresses RD significantly: keep step=1, document why."
#     B does not regress; ship.
#
# Skipped cells (default 2 GiB memory cap, symmetric across A and B —
# unrelated to fine_grained_step):
#   codec_wiki d=4.0 (A+B), imac_g3 d=2.0 (A+B), imac_g3 d=4.0 (A+B).
#   The cap fires in the chroma planner before AC strategy work, so the
#   missing cells don't bias the paired comparison.
